WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.569
Hi it's Michelle from Lab Muffin Beauty Science and my skin is annoyingly oily

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:10.980
if you have oily skin then you'll know
what a pain it is to deal with - makeup

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.769
slides off your face,
sunscreen slides around, everything

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:17.220
slides around and you spend a lot of
your time trying not to look like a

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.769
mirrorball. I've had so many people asking
me for my tips on how to deal with oily

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:32.399
skin so here it is! Oily skin is genetic
but sometimes if you're using the wrong

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:37.200
skin care products you can actually make
oily or even dry skin overproduce oil

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.719
and this gives you basically oilier skin
than you should have. Unfortunately some

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:48.239
of us like me are in the truly oily camp
or technically oily combo camp because

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:54.059
I've got oily t-zone and normal-ish
cheeks. Oily skin can also be dehydrated

00:00:54.059 --> 00:00:58.350
which leads to this weird dry but oily
situation where your skin feels like a

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.250
tight piece of leather and it's a bit
dry and maybe cracked but it's also

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.260
covered in a thin or thick layer of oil.
So a lot of people who think they have

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.740
dry skin - but there's still a whole bunch
of oil - you actually might have

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.150
dehydrated skin. The first thing to do if
you're frustrated with having oily skin

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.830
is to make sure you're not having that
situation. If you want a really detailed

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.759
guide on how to do a skin evaluation
and a rundown of all the different skin

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:28.380
types and conditions I've made one in my
guide to basic skin care. So let's say

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:38.189
your skin is actually oily - what can you
do? It's really tempting to wash your

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:42.420
skin with harsh cleansers to cut through
the oil and dry it out but don't do this

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.829
it is a trap

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.670
harsh cleansers will strip away both oil
and what's called your natural

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:55.590
moisturizing factor or NMF which is a
collection of chemicals that are in your

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.939
skin and these hold onto water and keep
it hydrated so it's like a natural

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:04.560
humectant moisturizer. Harsh surfactants
also warp the shape of some of the

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.099
proteins in your skin and this leads to
dehydration because it makes your skin

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:13.020
get leaky to water. Now, your skin is
responsive to its own hydration

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.130
level - when your skin's dehydrated it's
going to produce more oil to try to keep

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:24.600
your skin conditioned which means more oil.
Gentle cleansing is the way to go here.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.590
Your skin isn't meant to feel tight and
dry after you wash it. It should feel

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.550
soft and plump, almost like it's been
very lightly moisturized. If you're used

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.590
to really really dry clean skin after
washing then having properly washed skin

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.100
is going to feel a bit weird and it
might even feel like you haven't washed

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.970
properly for a bit - but if you persevere
you'll eventually get used to it and

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.110
your skin will be so much better for it.
Gentle cleansing was the number one

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:53.400
thing that helped my oily skin. There are
a lot of things that can go into finding

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.900
a gentle cleanser but the easiest thing
to do is to avoid sodium lauryl sulfate

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.300
in the top ingredients of your cleanser
and to also avoid soaps. The reason is

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.030
the molecules of these ingredients are
really skinny

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.050
so they insert themselves into your skin
quite easily sort of like a pin sliding

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:15.180
into your skin, and that means that they
stay in your skin and keep irritating it

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.690
even after you've washed it off. These
ingredients are also more stripping

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.320
which means they're more likely to take
away the oils and the NMF in your skin.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.550
Even gentle cleansers can cause some of
these effects which is why I recommend

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:31.500
that you try to clean your skin as
little as possible. So for me I only

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.300
cleanse my skin properly at night once a
day with cleanser. In the morning I just

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.959
use water - I splash my face with the
water and rub it around a bit and then

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:44.400
pat it dry with a towel. Using less
cleanser has helped my oily skin a lot. I

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.209
found that the oil tends to come back a
bit slower throughout the day instead of

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:52.500
sort of like just flooding my entire
face and it feels a lot more comfortable

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.810
so there isn't that weird tight feeling
and that whole greasy dehydrated flaky

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:05.250
shiny gross leathery situation has cut
back a lot. I've listed a couple of

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.360
gentle cleansers that I really like in
the caption but remember that everyone's

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.780
skin is different so it's really
important for you to work out what your

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.930
skin likes and how your skin responds to
different situations.

00:04:20.599 --> 00:04:24.960
It's really tempting to think that if
your skin is oily then it doesn't need

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.860
any more moisturizer because it's giving
itself way too much already but again

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:35.039
this is another trap. Your natural sebum
isn't actually that good at moisturizing.

00:04:35.039 --> 00:04:39.830
If your skin is hydrated and oily then
maybe you don't need another moisturizer

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:44.789
but if your skin's dehydrated and oily
which is the case for a lot of people

00:04:44.789 --> 00:04:50.009
then having a hydrating moisturizer that
addresses your dehydration issues with

00:04:50.009 --> 00:04:58.310
lots of occlusives and humectants - this
will help you control your oiliness.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:03.060
Salicylic acid which is commonly known
as beta hydroxy acid is a chemical

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.680
exfoliant and an anti inflammatory acne
treating skincare ingredient. It's

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.580
recommended for oily skin a lot because
it's oil soluble which means it's more

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.659
likely to be able to get through into
your blackheads and into your acne and

00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:20.520
clear them out. As far as I know there
haven't been actual studies on whether

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.870
or not this is true but it sounds pretty
reasonable. Oily skin tends to have

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.680
bigger pores and I've personally found
that my pores look a lot less noticeable

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:33.000
if I've been consistently using
salicylic acid for a while. The product I

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.439
use most of the time is Paula's Choice
2% BHA Liquid but there are a

00:05:37.439 --> 00:05:41.159
lot of options out there. And if you want
to find out more about exfoliation I've

00:05:41.159 --> 00:05:49.199
made a free guide that you can download
in the link below. Unfortunately there

00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:52.620
aren't that many skincare ingredients
that have been found to reduce the

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:57.210
amount of oil on your face and, for the
ones that there are, there's usually

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:02.939
like one single study on each of them so
it's probably not very reliable and they

00:06:02.939 --> 00:06:07.199
might not actually work. There's one
study where they used a 2 percent

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:11.599
niacinamide serum and this reduced the
amount of oil that was on people's faces.

00:06:11.599 --> 00:06:16.469
There's another study that found that a
plant extract of saw palmetto in a cream

00:06:16.469 --> 00:06:20.849
also reduced oiliness.
There's also vitamin A derivatives like

00:06:20.849 --> 00:06:25.229
retinol and tretinoin and these can
theoretically reshape the ducts that

00:06:25.229 --> 00:06:30.060
your oil comes out of and this slows
down how much it pulls out of your skin.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.840
You can also use a clay mask
to soak up any oil that's sitting

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.740
in your pores on your skin but you do
have to use these quite regularly so

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:42.300
that you keep the oil at bay. I find that
using it twice or three times a week is

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:50.790
necessary. I use a lot of translucent
powder for soaking up the oil on my skin

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:54.990
I use it pretty much every day if I
don't use it then there's no hope for me

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:59.580
the ingredient that I found the best for
this is starch so things like corn

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.590
starch rice starch arrowroot powder there's
tons and tons of starches I always look

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.250
for starch high up somewhere in the
ingredients list. Some translucent

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:12.270
powders also have clay which is also
pretty good at soaking up oil. One trick

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:16.020
that you can use for soaking up oil is
Wayne Goss's method which is where you

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:20.190
put a really light layer of powder under
your foundation so that you can soak up

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:24.270
the oil before it hits the surface so
before anyone can see it and so that

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.210
means that your foundation isn't going
to slide around as much because you've

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:36.090
just got this extra oil soaking powder
in there Multi sunscreening is my word

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:39.660
for using different sunscreens on
different parts of my face so for me

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:45.000
I've got lots of hyperpigmentation here
on the tops of my cheeks and they get

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.530
much much worse with like a tiny tiny
bit of Sun so I want a really protective

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:53.310
sunscreen on this area but the problem
is sunscreens with really high

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:57.360
protection tend to also be really greasy
and thick and uncomfortable so I don't

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.150
want to use the high protection
sunscreen everywhere because these bits

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.470
are gonna get super super greasy so what
I do is I put the normal sunscreen

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:09.240
everywhere and then I go back and I put
the high protection sunscreen on the

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.200
bits that need it. If you decide to do
this you need to make sure that you pat

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.310
your second sunscreen on really gently
to try to avoid shifting the lower layer

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:21.090
around too much. You also need to make
sure that the sunscreen ingredients are

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:25.590
actually compatible and they won't
interact with each other and just cancel

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:29.670
each other out. So for example I usually
use two Ultraceuticals sunscreens that

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:35.080
have the same active ingredients.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.080
Blotting papers are really really good
for getting rid of oil in the middle of

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:43.190
the day without messing up your makeup
too much just grab one of these and you

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.880
pat it on gently on the oily bits to
soak it up. My favourites are the thin

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.960
paper ones. I don't really like using the
plastic ones because it just feels like

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.220
I'm beating up Mother Nature when I use
them. You can also use toilet paper and

00:08:55.220 --> 00:09:03.980
napkins as well. It's been so ingrained
in my head over the years that matte is

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:09.710
the way to go with makeup for oily skin
but recently-ish I found that using dewy

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:14.660
makeup actually works better for me. The
reason is when I do get oily then the

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:18.740
contrast between the oily bits and the
non oily parts is a bit less obvious

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:23.300
than if I have the matte foundation and
if I have the matte foundation and I

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:28.160
have the oil then it looks really really
patchy. So I either look either kind of

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:35.720
glowy / slightly sweaty or just gross
and decomposing. I usually mix an

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.770
illuminating sort of fluid into my
foundation and then I add highlighter on

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:43.070
the tops of my cheeks and on the end of
my nose and a little bit on my nose as

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:48.050
well. Then I put the starch powder on top
and that seems to work pretty well. There

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:51.890
are a lot of anti-oil makeup products
and pore filling primers that have lots

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:56.150
of silicones in them but I've actually
personally found that too many silicones

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:00.620
make me look even worse. They look really
nice for about half an hour or so and

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:05.090
then the oil soaks into them and then
suddenly it all starts moving around on

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:11.790
my face and I look like I'm made of
melting wax

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:16.080
There are also some medical treatments
that can reduce oil production. Too many

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:20.700
androgens which are male sex hormones
can make you produce way too much oil

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:25.050
and there are some medications that can
reduce this so for example combined oral

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:29.220
contraceptive pills and spironolactone.
Isotretinoin which is also known as

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:34.650
accutane can also cut down on the oil.
Most of the time these prescription

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:39.960
medications aren't really used just for
treating oily skin but they are used for

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:44.400
acne, and reducing oil is one of the side
effects. If you're interested in these go

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.070
to your doctor and chat to them about
whether or not it's right for your

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:50.190
particular situation.
There are also some newer treatments and

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:54.270
ingredients that are promising for
treating oily skin so for example Botox

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.630
and laser and light treatments but
they're still pretty expensive at the

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:02.580
moment and the evidence behind them so
far isn't all that convincing. So those

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.780
are some of my tips for coping with oily
skin! Do you already use these? Do you

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:10.890
have a tip I didn't cover? Let me know
in the comments! If you liked my video

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:15.060
you can also subscribe to my channel. If
you want more regular beauty tips you

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:19.500
can follow me on Facebook and Instagram
I also have a blog where I have tons and

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.250
tons of articles on beauty products and
the science behind them. See you next time

